  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 107 PM CDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will shift slightly west on Tuesday, but still \nremain centered across New Mexico. This will result in another very \nhot day across the area, with highs in the upper 90s to near 108. A \nheat Advisory will likely be needed for the Big Country and portions \nof the Concho Valley and Heartland. \n\nWednesday and Thursday, the upper level ridge shifts a bit farther \nwest. This will result in \"less hot\" temperatures, but temperatures \nwill still remain well above seasonal normals. Highs on Wednesday \nwill be in the upper 90s to near 104, with highs on Thursday in the \nmid 90s to near 102. West Central Texas will be on the eastern \nperiphery of the ridge and the ECMWF and GFS are both indicating at \nleast isolated to scattered afternoon showers and thunderstorms \ndeveloping Wednesday and Thursday. For now have kept low rain \nchances (15-30%) in the forecast, but these may eventually need to \nbe increased some. Drier weather should return Friday int Saturday. \nHighs will continue to be above normal, in the upper 90s to near \n104. Overnight lows will mainly be in the 70s.",
